cfasl-4 — COMPILE-FILE / LOAD integration for the binary fasl (plan-1-compact-fasl).

Wire the binary format into the existing COMPILE-FILE / LOAD path.

WHAT
- COMPILE-FILE (bootstrap/prelude.lisp): keep the current compile-time processing
  (%COMPILE-FILE-TOPLEVEL: fire EVAL-WHEN :compile-toplevel, run IN-PACKAGE /
  DEFPACKAGE / DEFMACRO so later forms read/expand correctly), but instead of
  PRIN1'ing each MACROEXPAND-ALL'd form to a text stream, feed it to the cfasl
  writer (cfasl-2), emitting a binary fasl.  Emit the IN-PACKAGE pin + provenance
  as serialized forms (or header metadata).
- Choose the default: either the binary format becomes the default fasl (bump the
  fasl notion, keep the text writer available behind a flag/var for debugging), or
  gate by *DEFAULT-COMPILED-FILE-TYPE* / a switch.  Recommend: binary default.
- LOAD (prelude): peek the first bytes; dispatch to the binary loader (cfasl-3) on
  the binary magic, the text-source loader on the ";; BOCL <v> FASL" comment header
  or plain source, and keep the absent-fasl -> source fallback.
- Preserve: EVAL-WHEN :compile-toplevel effects at compile time; a compile-time
  IN-PACKAGE contained by the *PACKAGE* rebind; (values truename nil failure-p).

ACCEPTANCE: (load (compile-file "x")) works for single- and multi-package files with
DEFPACKAGE/IN-PACKAGE/DEFMACRO/DEFUN/DEFVAR; test_slice25 "compile-file *" still
green (adapt if the fasl is now binary — probe-file still finds it, LOAD still
works).

DEPENDS ON: cfasl-2, cfasl-3.  Interacts with [[bocl-fasl-format]] and the
minimal-compilation work (closed).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DONE (v1.6.4, cfasl branch).

Wired the binary format into COMPILE-FILE / LOAD.

C hooks (sources/bocl.c, registered as internal CL primitives):
  (%write-cfasl namestring forms)  -> T if a binary fasl was written, NIL if any
      form holds an object the writer can't serialize (nothing is written then).
      Each form gets a fresh writer context (per-form shared-object id space, to
      match the per-form reader); the whole image is built in memory, so a
      fallback never leaves a partial file.
  (%cfasl-file-p namestring)       -> T if the file starts with the BOCLFASL magic.
  (%cfasl-load  namestring)        -> bocl_fasl_load: T on success, NIL on
      not-a-cfasl / version mismatch.

COMPILE-FILE (bootstrap/prelude.lisp): unchanged compile-time pass
(%COMPILE-FILE-TOPLEVEL still fires EVAL-WHEN :COMPILE-TOPLEVEL / IN-PACKAGE /
DEFPACKAGE / DEFMACRO so later forms read + MACROEXPAND-ALL correctly), but now
COLLECTS each (package . macroexpanded-form) — capturing *PACKAGE* per form —
instead of printing immediately.  After the read loop it writes the collected
macro-free forms (preceded by an IN-PACKAGE load-package pin) via %WRITE-CFASL
(BINARY, the default per new *COMPILE-FILE-BINARY*), falling back to the new
%WRITE-TEXT-FASL when binary is disabled or %WRITE-CFASL returns NIL.  The text
writer prints each form under its OWN captured package, so multi-package files
still qualify symbols correctly on the text path.  Return value unchanged:
(values truename nil failure-p).

LOAD (prelude): do-load now dispatches by peeking the file — %CFASL-FILE-P ->
binary loader (with source-sibling fallback on a version mismatch); else the
existing ';; BOCL ... FASL' text-header path under controlled read syntax; else
source/foreign.  The absent-fasl -> source fallback is untouched.  EVAL-WHEN
:LOAD-TOPLEVEL, the *PACKAGE*/*READTABLE* rebind, and *LOAD-PATHNAME*/-TRUENAME
all behave as before (bocl_fasl_load binds the load vars identically).

ACCEPTANCE — verified:
  * test_slice25 "compile-file fasl" green, adapted to assert %CFASL-FILE-P (the
    binary default carries no text header) instead of %BOCL-FASL-VERSION; it still
    checks PROBE-FILE finds the file, LOAD works, and the loaded bodies are
    macro-free (no S25-DBL, no DOLIST).
  * Manual multi-package round-trip: a DEFPACKAGE + IN-PACKAGE + cross-package
    DEFUN + DEFMACRO + DEFVAR source compiles to a 1147-byte binary cfasl
    (cfasl?=T, no text header), (load (compile-file ...)) then gives
    greet=42 / cross-package caller=10 / flag=YES, macro fully expanded.
  * Text path: (setq *compile-file-binary* nil) writes a text-header fasl
    (cfasl?=NIL) that loads identically.
  * Auto-fallback: a file with a bignum literal writes a TEXT fasl (%WRITE-CFASL
    returned NIL) and loads correctly — never a wrong/partial file.
Full suite: see the cfasl-4 commit.
